{"affected":[{"original_ranges":[{"lessThan":"8.7.0","status":"affected","version":"0","versionType":"custom"}],"product":"Splunk Enterprise Security","vendor":"Splunk"}],"aliases":["CVE-2026-131201"],"assertions":[{"affected_indices":[0],"datePublic":"2026-11-18T00:00:00.000Z","descriptions":[{"lang":"en","value":"In Splunk Enterprise Security versions below 8.7.0, an unauthenticated user with network-path interception capability could cause attacker-controlled JavaScript to run in the browser of a security analyst who previews a Portable Document Format (PDF) attachment in Mission Control. The JavaScript could expose data and perform actions available to the security analyst.\nThe vulnerability is possible because Mission Control loads the PDF rendering worker from an external content delivery network.\nThe vulnerability requires the unauthenticated user to intercept the network path to the external content delivery network and a security analyst to preview a PDF attachment in Mission Control. The unauthenticated user should not be able to exploit the vulnerability at will.\nFor more information see Collaborate on investigations in Splunk Enterprise Security (https://help.splunk.com/en/splunk-enterprise-security-8/administer/8.7/investigations/collaborate-on-investigations-in-splunk-enterprise-security) in the Splunk documentation."}],"metrics":[{"cvssV3_1":{"baseScore":5.9,"baseSeverity":"MEDIUM","vectorString":"CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:U/C:H/I:L/A:N","version":"3.1"},"format":"CVSS","scenarios":[{"lang":"en","value":"GENERAL"}]}],"problemTypes":[{"descriptions":[{"cweId":"CWE-829","description":"The software imports, requires, or includes executable functionality (such as a library) from a source that is outside of the intended control sphere.","lang":"en","type":"cwe"}]}],"provider":{"dateUpdated":"2026-11-19T19:55:46.442Z","orgId":"d1c1063e-7a18-46af-9102-31f8928bc633","shortName":"cisco"},"role":"cna","title":"Cross-Site Scripting (XSS) through Mission 